KNOWNBUG
shared-loop-variable4.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.a == main\.b: PROVED up to bound 0$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^file .* line \d+: `Verilog::\$root\.main\.i' has multiple drivers$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The shared-loop-counter driver-conflict exemption in
verilog_rtl_buildert::commit (src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp) keys on the
declared type (ID_C_verilog_type == ID_integer). A loop index declared
'int' (as here), 'reg [N-1:0]' or 'logic [N-1:0]' is therefore NOT
exempted, so this benign shared counter is still reported as a spurious
driver conflict (the '--' section below is the current, buggy output).
Desired behaviour is PROVED, matching the 'integer' case in
shared-loop-variable2.sv. The principled fix is to exempt based on
liveness (index dead outside the loop) rather than on the type; see
Icarus Verilog bug #1000 and Yosys issue #295, both of which
discriminate on usage, not type.
